 a brilliant critic of art, photography, film, and dance. But behind this remarkably accomplished and renowned public face lay a complex, contradictory, often tortured human being. Kirstein suffered for decades from bipolar disorder, which frequently strained his relationships with his family and friends, a circle that included many notables, from W. H. Auden to Nelson Rockefeller. And despite being married for more than fifty years to a woman whom he deeply loved, Kirstein had a wide range of homosexual relationships throughout the course of his life.","primaryTopic":"Intellectual Biography","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Biography","confidence":"high","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Biography","score":8,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"llm_classifier","rawLabel":"Biography","mappedSubject":"Biography","score":8,"confidence":"high","note":"The book is primarily a biography of Lincoln Kirstein, discussing his life, contributions to the arts, and complex personal relationships, including his LGBTQ identity.","id":"subject-evidence-book-the-worlds-of-lincoln-kirstein-martin-duberman-1"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","rawLabel":"Biography & Autobiography","mappedSubject":"Memoir & Autobiography","score":7,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-open-library-the-worlds-of-lincoln-kirstein-martin-duberman","id":"subject-evidence-book-the-worlds-of-lincoln-kirstein-martin-duberman-7"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","rawLabel":"Biography / Autobiography","mappedSubject":"Memoir & Autobiography","score":7,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-open-library-the-worlds-of-lincoln-kirstein-martin-duberman","id":"subject-evidence-book-the-worlds-of-lincoln-kirstein-martin-duberman-9"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","rawLabel":"Biography/Autobiography","mappedSubject":"Memoir & Autobiography","score":7,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-open-library-the-worlds-of